========================================================================================================
(B) NECESSITY SCAN -- looking for LOW RANK carrying HIGH INFORMATION
========================================================================================================
RankMe's hedge: high rank is 'a necessary (but not sufficient) condition for good
downstream performance'. High-rank/low-information is therefore PREDICTED by the hedge
and is NOT a counterexample. Only the reverse breaks it.

PRE-DECLARED violation criterion (fixed before inspecting the pairs):
  a pair (lo, hi) is a violation iff  eff_rank(hi)/eff_rank(lo) >= 2.0
  AND  CCA(lo) - CCA(hi) >= 0.0705
  i.e. the LOWER-rank artifact carries at least as much more information as the
  smallest between-arm gap this project has accepted as real (D1 seed 42, +0.0705),
  while sitting at least 2.0x lower in rank.

  2 violating pair(s) of 66 examined:

     lower-rank artifact     rank      CCA   |  higher-rank artifact     rank      CCA      fold     dCCA  scope
                     P44   11.115   0.6087   |                   I43   34.117   0.4882     3.07x  +0.1206  cross-experiment
                     H44    9.143   0.5983   |                   I43   34.117   0.4882     3.73x  +0.1101  within-experiment, across arms

